# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
# A class needs only STEPFUN_API_KEY; DASHSCOPE_API_KEY (below) is optional.

# THE MAIN ONE. StepFun is the hackathon sponsor and sells most
# of what this product buys: the director (step-3.7-flash, bought direct rather
# than resold) and both voice slots (stepaudio-2.5-tts). Their platform lists 29
# models, 18 of them audio.
# Get a key at https://platform.stepfun.com — note that a key minted there works
# on api.stepfun.com ONLY; api.stepfun.ai answers and rejects it as "Incorrect
# API key provided", which reads as a bad key rather than as the wrong region.
#
# THERE IS A SUBSCRIPTION, and StepFun First runs on it: that
# deployment sends every StepFun call to https://api.stepfun.com/step_plan/v1
# instead of .../v1 (the pay-per-call address the archived API First used). ONE KEY
# SERVES BOTH — measured once, both addresses answered 200 to the same key
# — so nothing here needs changing for the plan. The two addresses list
# different models (10 against 36) and which models the studio uses:
# docs/guides/stepfun-plan-models.md
STEPFUN_API_KEY=

# StepFun First no longer needs this key: the DGX Spark now makes the
# moving clip (Wan 2.2 I2V A14B) itself, and the Mac + 4090 way that bought it here
# is archived. The development profiles (cloud, local) still read it. StepFun image
# models, including third-party hosted Step1X, are intentionally not configured.
# Get a token at https://replicate.com/account/api-tokens — billing can take a
# while to clear, so do this before you need it.
REPLICATE_API_KEY=

# Only for the `cloud` and `local` eval profiles' vlm.studio, which stands in for
# Step3-VL-10B with Qwen3-VL-8B. It existed for acceptance criterion B5 — the model
# that writes a critique must not grade its own work — because nobody, StepFun
# included, sells Step3-VL-10B as an API.
#
# B5 NO LONGER HOLDS FOR THE CLASSROOM. An operator decision runs all
# five roles in every shipping deployment on step-3.7-flash, separated by reasoning
# effort and by being separate requests, not by being separate models. See
# docs/history/three-deployment-execution-plan.md §1. The split survives only in
# evalkit, where writer and judge are still different slots, and that is the one
# place this key is still needed.
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# NOT NEEDED any more, and left here because the reason it existed still
# stands. SiliconFlow was the Chinese-payment route when a Replicate purchase sat
# "in progress" and stopped the work; StepFun is also Chinese, also takes that
# payment, and sells better models for both slots SiliconFlow held. The client in
# studio/providers/siliconflow.py still works and is tested, so a slot can be
# pointed back at it by editing a profile.
SILICONFLOW_API_KEY=

# NOT NEEDED. fal was the media route for one day early on and carried
# nothing Replicate lacks. The client in studio/providers/fal.py still works and
# is tested, so a slot can be pointed back at fal by editing a profile — but do
# not open an account for it without a reason.
FAL_KEY=

# OPTIONAL (operator): Alibaba's DashScope, for the online clip (Wan 3.0, 5 s
# in about 2 minutes; the drawing goes to Alibaba and the page says so). Leave it
# empty and the class makes its clips with Wan 2.2 on your own DGX Spark instead,
# 5 s in about 18 minutes: nothing else needs this key. With it, the Spark's clip
# is shown greyed, as on the node the project runs on, to keep its memory for a class.
# Get a key from Alibaba Cloud Model Studio (DashScope), China region.
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=

# NOT NEEDED: DeepInfra. It is cheaper per call and reports real costs, but it has
# no 3D model of any kind, so it cannot be the single media account. Checked once.
